he delta review. Executor [A497], on branch `pp141-clock-sources` at `76b09ff0` (round 2, REVIEW READY, pushed).\n\nProcessor `main` moved to `2ebd4fe8` (PR #139, lane C6, notifications and Identify). A trial merge has no text conflict. Both sides changed seven files:\n- `gen_ucode.py`;\n- `tb/pp_top/sim_main.cpp`, `pp_top_wrap.sv` and `README.md`;\n- `06_aecp_engine.md`, `09_verification.md` and `00_MILAN_COMPLIANCE_REVIEW.md`.\n\nC6 also moved two of its microprograms to ROM words 464 and 480. It adds builds to `tb/pp_top` and the notify campaign.\n\n**Items:**\n1. **Merge `main` `2ebd4fe8`** with a merge commit (`--no-ff`), never a rebase.\n   - Regenerate every ROM from its generator, and check for ROM-word overlaps beyond text: this lane's E_SCLKS changes against C6's words 464 and 480.\n   - Keep `tb/pp_top`'s builds numbered consistently everywhere (bench, README, 08/09, the campaigns).\n2. **Re-measure at the merge commit, targeted** (owner rule of 2026-10-02):\n   - Run `git apply --check` for every patch of every campaign. All must apply.\n   - Map the files the merge changes to the campaigns that read them, and re-run those campaigns. `tb/pp_top/sim_main.cpp` and the wrap are shared by every `tb/pp_top` campaign, so that means all of them: dispatch 37/37, D3 87/87, notify 40/40, AECP 55/55, ACMP 19/19, and the rest. No arm may be lost, and every count must match its README record.\n   - Run every processor suite.\n3. **Run the parent consumer gates** at milan-fpga dev `cdf49d1a` with the combined C4 + C6 parent patch (`parent-adoption-c4c6-ea3fb388.patch`), because `main` now carries C6. Run every gate whole if it fits. The manager's bank re-runs `test_builder.py` whole.\n\nSTOP on any port, parameter or parent-visible change.\n\n**Output:** add a \"Round 2b\" section to PR-BODY.md, and post REVIEW READY with the head. One delta review then covers rounds 2 and 2b.\n\nDo not edit or delete any existing comment.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"r